In commit "rpc: Properly throw on internal FindTx IO errors in ProcessPSBT and GetTransaction" (fa5c96a112c2d11e32278838cb43bae243f6e951)

Suggestion for a follow-up: skip index entries left behind by an unclean shutdown instead of throwing here and in the `BLOCK_HAVE_DATA` check below. Otherwise a crash at the wrong moment leaves some transactions permanently failing to look up with this error, even though nothing is corrupt, and the only way out is rebuilding the whole txindex.

The leftovers happen because [`WriteTxs`](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/fa87067c397814f79566f8e1b4f407745e3e1f8c/src/index/txindex.cpp#L113-L134) writes entries as soon as a block is connected, while the block index is only [flushed every 50–70 minutes](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/fa87067c397814f79566f8e1b4f407745e3e1f8c/src/validation.cpp#L98-L99). After a crash, the txindex can have entries for a block the node no longer knows about, or knows only as a header. If that block is connected again, everything lines up, but if it went stale in the meantime, its entries stay forever.

Such a block can't be in the active chain, so skipping its entries gives the same result as if it had never been indexed, which is what the code did before this PR. Missing data for a block that is in the active chain does mean corruption, and the change below still throws for that:

```diff
             LOCK(cs_main);
             const CBlockIndex* block_index{m_chainstate->m_blockman.LookupBlockIndex(candidate_block_hash)};
-            if (!block_index) {
-                WarnAndThrowErr(strprintf("%s: Block index entry %s not found for txid %s. Caused by data corruption or possibly an unclean shutdown?",
-                                          GetName(), candidate_block_hash.ToString(), tx_hash.ToString()));
-            }
+            // Entries are written as soon as a block is connected, before the
+            // block index is flushed, so after an unclean shutdown they can
+            // refer to a block whose index entry or data was never written.
+            // If the block was not connected again, it is not in the active
+            // chain, and skipping it gives the same result as if it had never
+            // been indexed. Only missing data for an active-chain block
+            // indicates corruption.
+            if (!block_index) continue;
+            const bool in_active_chain{m_chainstate->m_chain.Contains(*block_index)};
             if (!(block_index->nStatus & BLOCK_HAVE_DATA)) {
-                WarnAndThrowErr(strprintf("%s: Block data %s unexpectedly unavailable for txid %s. Caused by data corruption or possibly an unclean shutdown?",
+                if (!in_active_chain) continue;
+                WarnAndThrowErr(strprintf("%s: Block data %s unexpectedly unavailable for txid %s. Caused by data corruption?",
                                           GetName(), candidate_block_hash.ToString(), tx_hash.ToString()));
             }
             const FlatFilePos tx_position{block_index->nFile, block_index->nDataPos + key.pos.tx_offset_in_block};
-            candidates.emplace_back(tx_position, candidate_block_hash, key.pos.block_seq, m_chainstate->m_chain.Contains(*block_index));
+            candidates.emplace_back(tx_position, candidate_block_hash, key.pos.block_seq, in_active_chain);
```

